15g2|n|To breathe into; to fill with the breath; to animate. ; To infuse by breathing, or as if by breathing. ; To draw in by the operation of breathing; to inhale; -- opposed to expire. ; To infuse into the mind; to communicate to the spirit; to convey, as by a divine or supernatural influence; to disclose preternaturally; to produce in, as by inspiration. ; To infuse into; to affect, as with a superior or supernatural influence; to fill with what animates, enlivens, or exalts; to communicate inspiration to; as, to inspire a child with sentiments of virtue. ; To draw in breath; to inhale air into the lungs; -- opposed to expire. ; To breathe; to blow gently.	a:11rm,30,1~11rm,30,1	n:ofz,129,12;11rm,79,30~11rm,79,30;ofz,129,12
